SUMMARY:SMC Trail Work Volunteer Day
DESCRIPTION:South Mountain Conservancy Activities Meetup Group\n**TRAIL WO
 RK will continue rerouting the Hogenauer Trail** up the slope and away fro
 m recently installed property fences. **Meet At:** Dog Park/ Wildflower Pr
 eserve\, 11 Bear Lane\, Maplewood. From there\, we will walk to Crater Vie
 w on Crest drive and then to the Hogenauer trail work site.\n\nTrail work 
 is physically challenging but very satisfying as we use hand tools to buil
 d and repair trails. Participants must be 15+ years. Those younger than 18
  must be accompanied by an adult. Participants **should wear long pants** 
 due to [ticks](https://www.somocon.org/?page_id=193928&fb) and thron bushe
 s and sturdy shoes\, and bring gloves (though backup gloves will be availa
 ble). Tools\, water\, and a snack will be provided. (Registration is not r
 equired though if you sign up on Meetup\, it helps us know how many tools 
 to bring.) Only heavy\, steady rain cancels.
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/somocon/events/315845882/
STATUS:CONFIRMED
CREATED:20260726T161534Z
LAST-MODIFIED:20260726T161534Z
CLASS:PUBLIC
END:VEVENT
